# 🛑 Byte-exact, every one of them.
#
# These fixtures are asserted with `fileTypeFromBuffer` — the same detector
# /api/media/finalize uses — so a single changed byte moves a fixture from the
# happy path to the 422 rejection path, or the reverse. Either way the case still
# "passes" while testing something other than what its name says.
#
# `sample-doc.pdf` and `not-really-an-image.png` are pure ASCII, so git's autocrlf
# treats them as text and rewrites their line endings on checkout. For the PDF that
# is fatal and silent: its xref table stores absolute byte offsets, so a LF→CRLF
# conversion shifts every one of them and the file stops being a valid PDF on
# Windows only. Git warned about exactly these two on the commit that added them.
#
# The real images carry NUL bytes and git already leaves them alone; they are listed
# anyway so the rule does not depend on heuristics.
* -text -diff
